      "parts": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "\"When the Semantic Kernel library interacts with Azure OpenAI's Chat Completion endpoint, the response objects representing individual choices may not include a `logprobs` field. The existing implementation assumes this attribute is always present and attempts to read it directly, which leads to an `AttributeError` and crashes the calling code. The required behavior is to make the metadata extraction process robust: it should always produce a dictionary that contains a `logprobs` entry, but if the attribute is absent the value should be `None` rather than raising an exception. This handling must work for both standard chat completion choices and streaming chunk choices, ensuring that downstream components can safely access the metadata without needing to perform their own existence checks. The solution should not alter the public API contract; callers should continue to receive a metadata dictionary with the same keys, now safely populated. Additionally, the change must not introduce new warnings or errors and should preserve existing functionality for responses that do include the `logprobs` field.\"\n",
          "id": "prt_eee081b61001rrcjGhl0zBx2We",
          "sessionID": "ses_111f7e4b8ffe7yEWP4XVzGzZL7",
          "messageID": "msg_eee081b60001e8jbxQZfS5VYeE"
